# Line endings.
#
# Without this file the working copy's line endings depend on the machine:
# core.autocrlf=true (the default of a Windows Git install) rewrites every LF to
# CRLF on checkout, while a macOS/Linux checkout keeps LF. That difference is not
# cosmetic here — the blueprint compiler reads Markdown front matter, and a parser
# written against bare LF silently discards the whole front matter (site identity,
# theme tokens, nav) when it is handed CRLF. The same blueprint then compiles to a
# named site on one machine and to "Untitled" with no palette on another.
#
# Markdown is therefore pinned to LF everywhere. The compiler also tolerates both
# now, so this is defence in depth rather than the only guard.
*.md text eol=lf
